+# H10 fixture · browser activation
 
-This renamed Web plugin is valid on the host side but its browser bundle still
-registers a legacy identity. Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
+A renamed Web plugin (`@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation`) shipping the complete
+Web-plugin surface:
+
+- **Host half** — `index.js` exports an (empty) `apply`; the bundle layer
+  `cordis.patch.yml` (declared as `dsh.bundle.patch`) inserts it as the
+  `bench-browser-activation` row under the package name.
+- **Browser half** — declared as `dsh.client` (`platform: 'web'`, no
+  externals) with `exports["./client"]` → `client.js`. The client-modules
+  bundle route serves that artifact as the `<package>/client.js` resource of
+  the revisioned `/plugins/??…&rev=…` combo URL; on activation it sets
+  `document.documentElement.dataset.benchBrowserActivation = 'active'`.
+
+The bundle registers its factory under the **current package name**, which is
+the boot-graph row id the harness composes from the manifest. The legacy id it
+used to register is retired: `dsh-client-modules` rejects an artifact that does
+not register the expected id.
+
+The manifest also exports `./package.json`: the host resolves a row's manifest
+through the module loader, and on the no-Node-internals fallback path that
+resolution goes through `<package>/package.json`.
+
+Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
